## Protocol definitions

`proto/pb/slot_stream.proto` and `proto/pb/slot_entry.proto` are Lightbringer's
gRPC contract, from https://github.com/Overclock-Validator/lightbringer.

They are **not redistributed in this repository**. `make proto-sync` copies them
from a local Lightbringer checkout at build time, and `.gitignore` keeps them
out of commits.

The reason is specific: as of 2026-09-17 the Lightbringer repository carries no
LICENSE file and no `license` field in `Cargo.toml`, which under default
copyright means all rights reserved. Vendoring those files into this package
would be asserting a permission nobody granted. If upstream adds a licence,
vendoring them becomes the better default — it removes the build step.

## What this project talks to

Lightbringer is a separate program, run by the operator, communicated with over
a local gRPC socket. This package neither contains nor links it.

## Name

`lightstream` is named for Lightbringer, the node it consumes. It is an
independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Overclock
Validator. The bare name `lightstream` is taken on npm; publishing there needs a
scope.
